# kind: dynt-atoms
# description: Two edited fields returned by a client as EFIELD_2 (130) atoms echoing block/row/col with the new text, one per changed field (client-input.md §2).
# derivation: Each atom follows the etype-130 layout (PV-0651/PV-0652): flag1 u16 BE = 0, dlen = text byte length, mlen, maxnrchars u16 BE, then dlen text bytes at payload offset 6. atom_length = 13 + 6 + text (PV-0603). Header row/col echoed (PV-0610/PV-0611), attr 0x40 YES3D (PV-0626); dlg flags carried verbatim (0), not interpreted (#34). Atom 1 returns "42" at row 38; atom 2 returns "PONG" at row 41; both at block 5, col 47. Positions and values invented (D15; not the example client's block 1, col 20, IMPL-SS-1). No password field is used.
